33.steps:
1.Add a static DNS cache entry in DNS proxy;
2.Add a FQDN_PBR,the dst FQDN is the added static DNS cache entry's domian name,X3 is the outgoing interface;
3.On PC,ping the FQDN and capture the packet;
4.Change the static DNS cache entry's ip,on PC,flush dns cache and then ping the FQDN again,capture the packet.

32.steps:
1.Add a split DNS entry in DNS proxy;
2.Add a FQDN_PBR,the dst FQDN is the added split DNS entry's domian name,X3 is the outgoing interface;
3.On PC,ping the FQDN and capture the packet.

26.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR,X3 is the outgoing interface;
2.On PC,ping a host IP,such as 1.1.1.1,capture the packet;
3.Add the host IP 1.1.1.1 into the server,after this IP is resolved,ping 1.1.1.1 and capture the packet.

04.initial:
1.Add several FQDN AOs,host AOs and network AOs;
2.Add a group with FQDN AOs,host AOs and network AOs;
3.Add a PBR,select the added mixed AO group as the dst.

03.initial:
1.Add several FQDN AOs;
2.Add a group with several FQDN AOs;
3.Add a PBR,select the added group as the dst.

16.steps:
1.Add a VPN tunnel;
2.Add a FQDN_PBR,select the tunnel interface as the outgoing interface,check the ACL;
3.On PC,ping the FQDN,capture the packet.

27.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR;
2.Enable RIP or OSPF on X2 and router,check "Redistribute Static Routes";
3.Check the router's NSM.

25.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR,X3 is the outgoing interface;
2.On PC,ping an resolved host IP continuously,check the corresponding connection cache;
3.Delete this host IP from server,wait until the IP expired and the offset time elapsed,check the connection cache.

28.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR;
2.Enable RIP or OSPF on X2 and router,check "Redistribute Static Routes";
3.In diag page,enable the option "Advertise FQDN based policy route to dynamic routing protocol";
4.Check the router's NSM;
5.In DNS server,add a new resolved host ip ,after the host ip is resolved,check the router's NSM again.

14.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR,the dst is FQDN AO group,X3 is the outgoing interface;
2.On PC,ping a FQDN AO included in the group,capture the packet;
3.Delete this FQDN AO from the group,then ping this FQDN AO,capture the packet.
Note:In step 3,before ping the FQDN AO,need to manually flush connection cache or stop traffic and wait the connction cache expired.

07.initial:
1.In ipv4 view page,add a FQDN_PBR;
2.Change to ipv6 view page,add a FQDN_PBR;
3.Change to ipv4 and ipv6 view page,add a FQDN_PBR,select ip version.

24.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR,X3 is the outgoing interface;
2.On PC,ping the dst FQDN continuously,capture the packet;
3.Wait until the resolved IP expired but before the offset time,check the packet;
4.After the offset time elapsed,check the packet.

31.steps:
1.Add a static DNS cache entry in DNS proxy;
2.Add a FQDN_PBR,the dst FQDN is the added static DNS entry's domian name,X3 is the outgoing interface;
3.On PC,ping the FQDN and capture the packet.

35.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR,the outgoing interface is X3;
2.Download TSR;
3.On PC,ping any of the resolved host ip and capture the packet.
Note:In DNS server,there are at least 256 resolved host ip.

42.initial:
1.Add two FQDN AO, e.g. AO1, AO2, make sure AO1 can resolve one address, AO2 can resolve two addresses at first;
2.Adding two FQDN routing entries, one dst as AO1, another dst as AO2, gateway, interface, metric values are all same,check routing table;
3.Update DNS server configurations to make AO1 can resolve two addresses, AO2 can resolve only one;
4.In GUI AO page check AO1,AO2 resolved addresses get updated,check routing table.

23.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR,the dst is FQDN AO,X3 is the outgoing interface;
2.On PC,ping the FQDN,capture the packet;
3.Modify the FQDN AO,change its name or zone or hostname,ping the changed FQDN,capture the packet.

29.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR;
2.Enable RIP or OSPF on X2 and router,check "Redistribute Static Routes";
3.In diag page,enable the option "Advertise FQDN based policy route to dynamic routing protocol";
4.Check the router's NSM.
5.In diag page,disable the option "Advertise FQDN based policy route to dynamic routing protocol";
6.Check the router's NSM again.

36.steps:
1.Configure HA;
2.On active unit,add a FQDN_PBR,the dst is FQDN AO,X3 is the outgoing interface;
3.Change any option of the FQDN_PBR or delete this FQDN_PBR in the active unit;
4.On PC,ping the dst FQDN,capture the packet in the active unit;
5.Force active/standby failover,on PC,ping the dst FQDN,capture the packet.

41.initial:
1.Add a FQDN AO,enable "Manually set DNS entries' TTL" and set TTL to 150;
2.Add a PBR,select the added FQDN AO as the dst;
3.On PC,ping the dst FQDN and check if resolved hosts with TTL 150;
4. Wait for TTL expired and offset time elapsed,ping the dst FQDN again,check if resolved hosts with TTL 150.

15.steps:
1.Add a PBR,the dst is AO group,X3 is the outgoing interface;
2.Add another FQDN AO;
3.On PC,ping the added FQDN,capture the packet;
4.Add this added FQDN AO into the group,then ping the FQDN again,capture the packet.

38.initial:
1.Add several FQDN_PBRs;
2.Export prefs and restart the DUT with factory default;
3.Import the prefs.

34.steps:
1.Add a split DNS entry in DNS proxy;
2.Add a FQDN_PBR,the dst FQDN is the added split DNS entry's domian name,X3 is the outgoing interface;
3.On PC,ping the FQDN and capture the packet;
4.Change the split DNS entry's server,after the dns cache expired,on PC,ping the FQDN again and capture the packet.

37.steps:
1.Configure HA and enable stateful synchronization;
2.On active unit,add a FQDN_PBR,the dst is FQDN AO,X3 is the outgoing interface;
3.Change any option of the FQDN_PBR or delete this FQDN_PBR in the active unit;
4.On PC,ping the dst FQDN,capture the packet in the active unit;
5.Force active/standby failover,on PC,ping the dst FQDN,capture the packet.

19.steps:
1.Add a FQDN_PBR,ensure no host can be resolved,X3 is the outgoing interface;
2.On PC,ping the FQDN,capture the packet;
3.In DNS server add a host,after the FQDN AO get resolved,ping the FQDN and capture the packet.

19.result:
In step 1,verify the PBR should be gray out when no host can be resolved;
In step 2,check the packet,the outgoing interface is X1(the default WAN);
In step 3,verify the grayed FQDN PBR could change active again once the FQDN AO get resolved and check the packet,the outgoing interface is X3.
